ind Assistant after months of struggling through clunky onboarding with other tools 🙌 \n\nThe setup was SO smooth—literally got productive in like 20 mins instead of spending hours decoding tutorials. As someone juggling a day job + side hustle, I don't have time to waste on confusing UX 😤\n\nGame changer for my workflow tbh. Worth every penny 💯\n\n#NovaMindAssistant #SideHustleTools #ProductivityHack", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S1', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': 'Alex Chen'}, {'post_id': 331, 'day': 140, 'content': "ugh been using NovaMind for like 2 months and honestly? the community around it is kinda dead 💀 barely any templates, guides, or people sharing wins. tried searching for workflow tips and got nothing. for the price point it's frustrating bc you'd think there'd be more users swapping ideas but it feels like you're just... alone with the tool lol\n\nswitched to the free tier anyway since the premium features weren't worth the grind. would rather spend time figuring stuff out myself than pay for vibes that don't exist yet #SaveYourCash #SaaShipwreck", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S1', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': 'Jordan Taylor'}, {'post_id': 330, 'day': 140, 'content': "ugh okay so i've been using NovaMind Assistant for like 3 weeks and honestly? not hitting different 💀 \n\nswitched from ChatGPT because the price seemed way better for side hustles but the output quality is... mid. takes me longer to edit responses than if i just wrote stuff myself lmaooo. that's literally cutting into my hourly rate 📉\n\nfor budget gigs maybe it works but if you're trying to actually *make money* the time investment isn't worth the savings imo. back to the drawing board 🤷\u200d♀️\n\n#GigEconomy #SaaS #NotWorthIt", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S1', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_n